						<main id="main-content" class="asic-page__main">
								<header class="asic-page__header">
									<!-- Page header component goes here -->						
									<h1 class="asic-text-title-large">
										Registered agent portal access
									</h1>
								</header>							

							<div class="asic-page__article">
								
								<!-- Prose component goes here -->								
<p class="intro">If you’re a registered agent for companies, you can use the registered agent portal to see company details and to complete common lodgements on their behalf.</p>
<h2>Quick links</h2>
<div class="container">
<div class="inside">
<h3>Portal access</h3>
<a href="https://www.edge.asic.gov.au/001/regaportal/get/ServicesLogin" class="asic-button asic-button--primary">Log in</a> <a href="https://www.edge.asic.gov.au/cgi-bin/Lodgement/RC99V004/start/ApplicationLogin" class="asic-button asic-button--secondary">Sign up</a></div>
<div class="inside">
<h3>Support</h3>
<a href="#user-guides" class="asic-button asic-button--secondary">User guides</a></div>
</div>
<p>You will need your ASIC registered agent number, username and password to log in.</p>
<h2>Before you start</h2>
<p>To use the registered agent portal, you need to:</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="#ra-number" data-anchor="#ra-number">get a registered agent number</a></li>
<li><a href="#elp" data-anchor="#elp">read ASIC's Electronic Lodgement Protocol</a></li>
<li><a href="#steps-sign-up" data-anchor="#steps-to-register">sign up for the registered agent portal</a></li>
</ul>
<!-- ACCORDION START -->
<div class="accordion accordion-expand">
<h3><a id="ra-number"></a>Registered agent number</h3>
<p>To sign up for the registered agent portal, you must first <a href="/for-business-and-companies/companies/registered-agents-for-companies/act-as-a-registered-agent-for-companies/#steps-agent" data-anchor="#steps-agent">apply to be a registered agent</a>.</p>
<p>If your application is accepted, we’ll send you an <strong>ASIC registered agent number</strong>. You need this number to sign up for the portal.</p>
<h3><a id="elp"></a>ASIC’s Electronic Lodgement Protocol</h3>
<p>Before signing up, read ASIC's <a href="/online-services/online-services-information-and-support/electronic-lodgement-protocol" title="Electronic lodgement protocol">Electronic Lodgement Protocol</a>. The protocol includes ASIC’s requirements for storing signed documents that you lodge online.</p>
<h3><a id="steps-sign-up"></a>Steps to sign up for the registered agent portal</h3>
<!-- SEQUENCE START -->
<div class="asic-sequence">
<div class="asic-sequence__section">
<h4 class="asic-sequence__title asic-text-title">Start creating your account</h4>
<ul>
<li>Go to the <a href="https://www.edge.asic.gov.au/cgi-bin/Lodgement/RC99V004/start/ApplicationLogin">sign-up page</a>.</li>
<li>If you agree to the protocol select ‘Yes’. If you do not agree and select ‘No’ you will not be able to sign up.</li>
<li>For the question ‘On what basis are you applying?’, select ‘as an ASIC registered agent’ from the list of options.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="asic-sequence__section">
<h4 class="asic-sequence__title asic-text-title">Enter your ASIC registered agent number</h4>
<p>Enter your registered agent number, then select the ‘Next’ button.</p>
</div>
<div class="asic-sequence__section">
<h4 class="asic-sequence__title asic-text-title">Enter username, password and security question and answer</h4>
<ul>
<li>Your password must:
<ul>
<li>be 16 to 50 characters long</li>
<li>include at least one lowercase letter (a–z), one capital letter (A–Z) and one number (0–9).</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>For your security question, choose something you will remember the answer to. If you lose your password and forget the answer to your security question, you will need to create a new account.</li>
<li>Enter all details and select the ‘Next’ button. A pop-up box will appear. Enter your username and password again, then select the ‘Next’ button.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="asic-sequence__section">
<h4 class="asic-sequence__title asic-text-title">Enter contact email address and phone number</h4>
<ul>
<li>Choose an email address that you use often. We use this email address to tell you that we’ve sent correspondence to your online inbox in this portal.</li>
<li>Enter your name, email address and phone number, then select the ‘Next’ button.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="asic-sequence__section">
<h4 class="asic-sequence__title asic-text-title">Confirm annual statement package information</h4>
<ul>
<li>Once you create an online account, ASIC will send annual statements to your online inbox for companies that appoint you as a registered agent.</li>
<li>Tick the box to say you understand this, then select the ‘Next’ button.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="asic-sequence__section">
<h4 class="asic-sequence__title asic-text-title">Print, sign and send</h4>
<p>You will need to print and sign a participation agreement and email it to <a href="mailto:agent.registration@asic.gov.au">agent.registration@asic.gov.au</a>. Once you have submitted the agreement, select ‘Yes’ and then ‘Next’.</p>
</div>
<div class="asic-sequence__section">
<h4 class="asic-sequence__title asic-text-title">Declare and submit</h4>
<ul>
<li>Fill in the declaration details, then select the 'Submit' button.</li>
<li>You'll see a screen confirming your request has been submitted.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="asic-sequence__section">
<h4 class="asic-sequence__title asic-text-title">Activate your online account</h4>
<p>ASIC will contact you within 2 business days to confirm your account has been activated.</p>
</div>
</div>
<!-- SEQUENCE END --><strong>Portal user guide</strong>
<p>For more detailed information and screenshots, see our user guide:</p>
<p><a href="https://download.asic.gov.au/media/a0gmnsxj/ra_how-to-sign-up-for-online-access-202507.pdf" title="How to sign up for online access (PDF 2.3 MB)">How to sign up for online access (PDF 2.3 MB)</a></p>
<p><a href="https://download.asic.gov.au/media/304lwdbp/ra_how-to-use-the-registered-agent-portal-202507.pdf" title="RA User Guide How to use the registered agent portal (July 2025)">How to use the registered agent portal (PDF 1.3 MB)</a></p>
</div>
<h2><a id="user-guides"></a>What you can do using the registered agent portal</h2>
<p>You can do the following tasks on the registered agent portal. Select a heading to see user guides and links for each task.</p>
<!-- ACCORDION START -->
<div class="accordion accordion-expand">
<h3>Link a company to your account</h3>
<h4>Portal user guides</h4>
<p><a href="http://download.asic.gov.au/media/1192208/ra-user-guide-appoint-or-cease-ra.pdf">How to appoint or cease a registered agent (PDF 733 KB)</a></p>
<p><a href="http://download.asic.gov.au/media/2650208/ra-user-guide-agent-ceasing-to-act.pdf">How to notify ASIC that you are ceasing to act as the registered agent for a company (PDF 1.4 MB)</a></p>
<h4>More information</h4>
<p>To link a company to your online account, the company must confirm they have appointed you as a registered agent. They must do this by completing the following form:</p>
<p class="form-link"><a href="/regulatory-resources/forms/forms-folder/362-notification-by-a-company-to-nominate-or-cease-a-registered-agent-or-contact-address" title="362 Notification by a company to nominate or cease a registered agent or contact address">Form 362 <em>Notification by a company to nominate or cease a registered agent or contact address</em></a>.</p>
<p>You must have a paper copy of the form signed by an officeholder of the company. You can then lodge the form via the registered agent portal. The company will be linked to your account once the form has been processed.</p>
<h3>Check company details and forms you have submitted</h3>
<h4>Portal user guide</h4>
<p><a href="http://download.asic.gov.au/media/1192316/user-guide-registered-agents.pdf">Check and change company details online – full user guide (PDF 6.3 MB)</a></p>
<h4>More information</h4>
<p>Forms you have submitted via the portal will only be available for 90 days.</p>
<h3>Process annual review</h3>
<h4>Portal user guides</h4>
<p><a href="http://download.asic.gov.au/media/3327417/ra-user-guide-request-for-ad-hoc-company-statement.pdf">How to request an ad hoc company statement (PDF 754 KB)</a></p>
<p><a href="http://download.asic.gov.au/media/3327423/ra-user-guide-review-date-report.pdf">How to request a list of company review dates (PDF 658 KB)</a></p>
<p><a href="http://download.asic.gov.au/media/3327375/ra-user-guide-company-debt-report.pdf">How to submit a request for a company debt report (PDF 686 KB)</a></p>
<p><a href="https://download.asic.gov.au/media/2650213/ra-user-guide-statement-in-relation-to-company-solvency.pdf">How to lodge a statement in relation to company solvency (PDF 867 KB)</a></p>
<h4>More information</h4>
<p>If you are the registered agent for a company, the annual statement will be sent to you, <strong>not</strong> the company officeholders.</p>
<h3>Change company details</h3>
<h4>Portal user guides</h4>
<p><a href="http://download.asic.gov.au/media/1192214/ra-user-guide-change-company-details-change-of-address.pdf">How to change company details – change of address (PDF 1.0 MB)</a></p>
<p><a href="https://download.asic.gov.au/media/5979817/ra-user-guide-change-company-details-change-of-details-appoint-or-cease-company-officeholder.pdf">How to change company details – appoint or cease company officeholders (PDF 1.6 MB)</a></p>
<p><a href="http://download.asic.gov.au/media/1192226/ra-user-guide-change-company-details-change-of-details-ultimate-holding-company.pdf">How to change company details – ultimate holding company (PDF 938 KB)</a></p>
<p><a href="https://download.asic.gov.au/media/1192232/ra-user-guide-change-company-details-change-of-name-officeholders-or-members.pdf">How to change company details – change of name (officeholders or members) (PDF 1.0 MB)</a></p>
<p><a href="https://download.asic.gov.au/media/1192238/ra-user-guide-change-company-details-change-to-members-register.pdf">How to change company details – change to members register (PDF 1.5 MB)</a></p>
<p><a href="https://download.asic.gov.au/media/1192244/ra-user-guide-change-company-details-change-to-share-structure.pdf">How to change company details – change to share structure (PDF 1.3 MB)</a></p>
<p><a href="https://download.asic.gov.au/media/1192250/ra-user-guide-change-company-details-change-to-special-purpose-status.pdf">How to change company details – change to special purpose status (PDF 959 KB)</a></p>
<p><a href="https://download.asic.gov.au/media/1192280/ra-user-guide-notification-of-resolution-change-to-company-name.pdf">How to submit a notification of resolution (change of company name) (PDF 927 KB)</a></p>
<p><a href="https://download.asic.gov.au/media/2650210/ra-user-guide-notification-of-supplementary-information.pdf">How to notify ASIC of supplementary information (PDF 813 KB)</a></p>
<p><a href="https://download.asic.gov.au/media/2650211/ra-user-guide-request-for-correction.pdf">How to lodge a request for correction (PDF 815 KB)</a></p>
<p><a href="https://download.asic.gov.au/media/5979823/ra-user-guide-resignation-or-retirement-of-an-officeholder.pdf">How to notify ASIC that a company officeholder has resigned or retired (PDF 1.4 MB)</a></p>
<h4>More information</h4>
<p>You can lodge a change of company details even if you have not been appointed as the company’s registered agent. To do this, you will need the company’s corporate key as well as your login details. The corporate key can be found:</p>
<ul>
<li>on the cover letter sent when the company was registered</li>
<li>on the most recent annual statement.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Deregister a company</h3>
<h4>Portal user guide</h4>
<p><a href="http://download.asic.gov.au/media/1192256/ra-user-guide-how-to-apply-for-voluntary-deregistration.pdf">How to apply for voluntary deregistration (PDF 833 KB)</a></p>
<h4>More information</h4>
<p>You can apply for <a href="/for-business-and-companies/companies/company-deregistration-and-winding-up/voluntary-deregistration-of-a-company" title="Voluntary deregistration of a company">voluntary deregistration</a> even if you have not been appointed as the company’s registered agent. To do so, you will need the company’s corporate key as well as your login details. The corporate key can be found:</p>
<ul>
<li>on the cover letter sent when the company was registered</li>
<li>on the most recent annual statement.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Reserve a company name</h3>
<h4>Portal user guides</h4>
<p><a href="http://download.asic.gov.au/media/2650209/ra-user-guide-application-for-reservation-of-a-name.pdf">How to apply to ASIC to reserve a company name for an existing company (PDF 1.2 MB)</a></p>
<p><a href="https://download.asic.gov.au/media/4137828/ra-user-guide-extension-of-name-reservation.pdf">How to extend the reservation of a company name (PDF 1.2 MB)</a></p>
<h3>Lodge forms</h3>
<p>Where a form can be lodged online, registered agents must use the portal. User guides are available to assist you with lodgements.</p>
<p><strong>Portal user guides</strong></p>
<p><a id="sustainability-report-registered-agent"></a><a href="https://download.asic.gov.au/media/waliwvsi/user-guide-how-to-lodge-a-sustainability-report-and-auditor-s-report-registered-agent-portal.pdf" title="User Guide How To Lodge A Sustainability Report And Auditor's Report Registered Agent Portal">How to lodge a sustainability report and auditor’s report - Registered agent portal (PDF 2.2 MB)</a></p>
<p><a href="https://download.asic.gov.au/media/4137827/copy-of-financial-statements-and-reports.pdf">How to lodge financial statements and reports (PDF 1.7 MB)</a></p>
<p><a href="https://download.asic.gov.au/media/4137830/registered-agent-user-guide-how-to-submit-an-application-for-registration-of-a-managed-investment-scheme.pdf">How to register a managed investment scheme (PDF 1.2 MB)</a></p>
<p><a href="https://download.asic.gov.au/media/4137829/registered-agent-user-guide-how-to-submit-a-pds-in-use-notice.pdf">How to submit a PDS in-use notice (PDF 2.0 MB)</a></p>
<p><a href="https://download.asic.gov.au/media/3327405/ra-user-guide-how-to-submit-notice-of-change-to-fees-and-charges-in-a-pds.pdf" title="Ra User Guide How To Submit Notice Of Change To Fees And Charges In A Pds">How to submit a notice of change to fees and charges in a PDS (PDF 962 KB)</a></p>
<p><a href="http://download.asic.gov.au/media/3327411/ra-user-guide-how-to-submit-notice-that-a-product-has-ceased-to-be-available.pdf">How to submit notice that a product in a PDS has ceased to be available (PDF 892 KB)</a></p>
<h3>Ask to lodge forms by email if you have issues</h3>
<!-- CALLOUT BOX START -->
<div class="asic-callout asic-callout--caution">
<h4 class="asic-callout__title">Mailbox closing</h4>
<div class="asic-callout__content">
<p><strong>From 12 October 2026</strong>, the <a href="mailto:online.exceptions@asic.gov.au">online.exceptions@asic.gov.au</a> mailbox will be decommissioned.</p>
<p>See <a href="/for-business-and-companies/forms-and-fees/how-to-lodge-forms-online-email-mail#email" title="How to lodge forms: online, email, mail" data-anchor="#email">How to lodge forms: online, email, mail</a> for the list of forms that can be lodged by email or explore alternative lodgement options.</p>
</div>
</div>
<!-- CALLOUT END -->
<p>The following forms cannot always be easily lodged online:</p>
<ul>
<li><em>Changes to company details</em> (formerly Form 484)</li>
<li>Form 362 <em>Notification by a company to nominate or cease a registered agent or contact address</em></li>
<li>Form 6010 <em>Application for voluntary deregistration of a company</em></li>
<li>Form 205A <em>Notification of resolution to change company name.</em></li>
</ul>
<p>If you have issues, you can request to lodge these forms via email. To do this you must be a registered agent, and be registered to use the agent portal or third-party software.</p>
<p>To apply for email lodgement, email <a href="mailto:online.exceptions@asic.gov.au">online.exceptions@asic.gov.au</a> with details of why you cannot lodge online and copies of any error screens or messages you’ve received.</p>
<p>If we agree with your request, we’ll send you a copy of the relevant form with further instructions. You’ll need to return this to the same email address, as well as a <a href="https://download.asic.gov.au/media/3829766/request-to-lodge-documents-via-email.doc">Request to lodge documents via email (DOC 113 KB)</a>.</p>
<p>You’ll need to include your registered agent number and the company’s corporate key if you’re lodging a change to company details or Form 362. The corporate key can be found:</p>
<ul>
<li>on the cover letter sent when the company was registered</li>
<li>on the most recent annual statement.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<h2>What you cannot do using the registered agent portal</h2>
<p>You cannot do the following tasks on the registered agent portal. Select a heading to see more information.</p>
<!-- ACCORDION START -->
<div class="accordion">
<h3>Change your details as a registered agent</h3>
<p>You can only use the portal to make changes involving companies. You cannot use it to update your own details as a registered agent. To learn how to update these details, see <a href="/for-business-and-companies/companies/registered-agents-for-companies/act-as-a-registered-agent-for-companies" title="Act as a registered agent for companies">Act as a registered agent for companies</a>.</p>
</div>									


							</div>

							
